nodecode-dogmatic-skill-router is a rewrite of DoGMaTiiC's DoGMaTiiC/hermes-jev:

  https://github.com/DoGMaTiiC/hermes-jev
  commit 5dddbeaac5be08281e6c3b372eeaba3639971f0a (plugins/jev-dogmatic-skill-router)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Patrick / DoGMaTiiC (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the two-request decision (one choice over the whole roster plus
three gate questions, then a re-read of the shortlist with each candidate's
own text and one fits question each), its thresholds, its chunking at 240
options, the skip rules, the one injected line, and the three wire routes
(TypeSafe's /v1/systemone, OpenRouter's Decisions API, the Vercel AI
Gateway's evaluation-model) with the same defaults, key order and
fail-open posture. The Hermes hook and the roster changed with the host: the
pre_llm_call hook became an advice on the one in-process ingress plus an
advice on where a turn's standing sections are read, the <skill_relevance>
block became the harness section of that name, and the SKILL.md walk became
the organism's own kept prose skills, which the core reads as data.

Left out: the plugin's CLI verbs that only made sense against Hermes's own
config and log (on/off/auto wrote config.yaml; status and check reported the
JSONL decision log), its Hermes credential-pool and .env lookup for the
OpenRouter key, its Retry-After retry and per-endpoint pacing, and its
per-process response cache. The cell reads auth.json and the environment,
keeps a failure breaker, and speaks its state through /dogmatic-skill-router instead
of writing a log.
